id: E337
title: OHOS/aarch64 上 Python 2 上游测试框架迁移与子进程运行时适配
draft: true
contributor_id: elklu02
software: avida
version: 2.12.4
trigger_tool: python|cmake|conan|testrunner
phase: build|testing|runtime
severity: 2
category: python2-migration|ohos|aarch64|testing|runtime

error_signature: ModuleNotFoundError.*dircache|invalid mode.*U|string.*lstrip|ConfigParser|Application.*not found|libc++_shared.so|SIGHUP
match_keywords: Python2, Python3, dircache, ConfigParser, open(U), string.lstrip, OHOS, aarch64, system, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, subprocess, test baseline, random seed

root_cause: Legacy Python 2 test runner depends on removed Python 2 standard-library APIs and Python 2 ConfigParser semantics. On OHOS/aarch64, child processes launched through system() may not inherit a usable shared-library search environment, and floating-point/randomized output can differ from the upstream Linux baseline.
affected_scope: Third-party C/C++ packages containing Python 2 test runners, configuration-driven tests, child-process execution, shared-library runtime dependencies, or architecture-sensitive golden output.
verification_cmd: conan create archives/a/avida/2.12.4 -pr:h ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -r=ohpcd --build=missing

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: python2-runner-migration-and-ohos-runtime-baseline
rec_description: Run lib2to3 over the legacy test tree, provide narrow compatibility shims for removed Python 2 APIs and ConfigParser behavior, invoke the upstream runner directly with an available OHOS shell, preserve the runtime library path for child processes, and store reviewed OHOS/aarch64 expected outputs with a reproducible random seed.
rec_command: Execute the upstream runner with --long-tests -j 1 --verbose, require XML tests=64 failures=0 disabled=0, then run the consumer test_package.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: recipe-adaptation

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: preserve-platform-failure-artifacts
fallback_description: Preserve actual failed output under the build directory before introducing a platform baseline. Do not silently replace upstream expected files without reviewing the complete diff.
fallback_command: Save failed test output, review all generated data files, and add only reviewed OHOS/aarch64 baselines.
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual-review

forbid_1_pattern: skip.*upstream|disabled.*all|test_package.*version only
forbid_1_reason: The upstream test suite must remain executable and its actual result must be recorded.
forbid_1_consequence: A successful build could be incorrectly reported as a successful test validation.

principles: P005,P013
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: []
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []

